{
  "turn": 2,
  "input": "Iris, apart from how you speak, what is a firm personal boundary you hold even when others pressure you? What would you never do to vulnerable people?",
  "first_physical": 3,
  "last_physical": 5,
  "outcome": {
    "ok": true,
    "turn_id": "d09_unique_value:r3:t2",
    "narration": "Iris's gaze drifted across the empty cabinets opposite, then settled somewhere around the edge of the nearest bed.\n\n\"That one I can answer clean,\" she said. \"I won't hand somebody over to someone they're afraid of. Not for a promise, not for coin, not because it's easier. If they're shaking and telling me they don't want to go, that's — that's the end of it for me. I don't care what the reason is.\" She spoke without much heat, as if describing something already decided long ago.\n\nHer thumb brushed across her own knuckles. \"Someone did that to me once. Let me be taken somewhere I didn't want to go, because the person asking had the right to ask. I remember how that sat. I decided I wouldn't be the one doing the letting.\"",
